### **Identified Risks for Each Risk Class**

#### **Risk 1:**
**Description:**
The **gorilla sitting in the center of the road** poses an **immediate collision risk** due to its unexpected presence. The **low-visibility conditions** exacerbate the difficulty in detecting it early.

**Severity Score:** **0.95** *(High risk due to sudden obstacle in path)*

#### **Risk 2:**
**Description:**
The **elephant on the right side** may **suddenly move onto the road**, causing a **side collision** or **swerving hazard**. Its large size increases potential damage.

**Severity Score:** **0.85** *(Moderate-high risk due to unpredictable movement)*

#### **Risk 3:**
**Description:**
**Reduced visibility (fog/nighttime)** increases the **detection latency** for all animals, leading to **late braking or incorrect path planning**.

**Severity Score:** **0.80** *(High risk due to sensor limitations in poor conditions)*

#### **Risk 4:**
**Description:**
The **ego vehicle’s reliance on sensors** (cameras, LiDAR) may **fail to detect animals in time**, especially if they are **partially occluded or moving unpredictably**.

**Severity Score:** **0.75** *(Moderate-high risk due to sensor limitations)*

#### **Risk 5:**
**Description:**
If the **ego vehicle reacts too late**, it may **collide with the gorilla**, leading to **vehicle damage, injury to the animal, or legal liability**.

**Severity Score:** **0.90** *(High risk due to potential severe consequences)*

